/-!
# The Theory of Becoming: the formal core

One relational unfolding, stated once. The core is the foundation (`GenerativeCore`,
`InquirySufficiency`, `RelationalRenewal`) and four layers:

* `Becoming.Frame` (L1): a frame is a process with realized claims; runs,
  reachability, invariants and new realization.
* `Becoming.Inquiry` (L2): the visible scope of an inquiry is what its actual
  executions reach; a sound policy secures its goal there.
* `Becoming.Recurrence` (L2): what every law of change keeps, loses and returns to, with
  no premise and no decidability. A list holding enough of a sequence holds two equal values;
  within finitely many configurations a law merges nothing exactly where every configuration
  returns, a rise needs a merge, and a merge loses a possibility for good; keeping its history,
  every law loses nothing, never returns and needs an open world, while a finite present
  forgets.
* `Becoming.Renewal` (L3): every run read through conditions is one relational
  unfolding; renewal and consumption belong to the run.
* `Becoming.Dependence` (L3): dependence forms, holds, breaks and dissolves across
  steps; the outcomes of a loss where activity needs support; stepwise readings of
  events and their relations; the arithmetic the layers share.
* `Becoming.Return` (L3): renewal graded by the time to return; readings over cycles.
* `Becoming.Horizon` (L3): no finite stretch of a run decides whether its drawing
  renews or consumes in the whole-run sense, with or without feedback; a reading of
  amounts is decided step by step.
* `Becoming.Joint` (L3): difference-making, relative to a move that can still be taken
  once a part is withheld and read as intended when the move determines the step,
  belongs to the joint activity among formations; over a formation's events the run-level outcome is
  fixed by the tail, while the step-level test singles out the breaking event.
* `Becoming.Experiment` (L3): what varying one's own act tests, and what it needs. Relative
  to determinacy, the record fixes what a move does at a configuration exactly where the run
  has taken it there; what one's act would have done otherwise is fixed only where the
  configuration returns, and a kept history never returns. Read through a projection the step
  factors through, one occasion stands for its whole class; a wrong projection misattributes,
  is never refuted by moves in step with what it leaves out, and is refuted by moves varied
  against it. The readings are the AI's, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Substitution` (L3): in the support-gated law, a consumer that substitutes
  a condition persists and still consumes on the whole-run reading, while the stepwise
  reading credits it until the sustaining formation loses support and withholds it from
  then until it switches.
* `Becoming.Generation` (L3): formations arise. Where arising depletes a finite family
  of conditions, unceasing generation needs their renewal to recur; renewal does not
  imply generation; substitution among unrenewed conditions defers the end; and
  dissipation ends generation, while a closed cycle need not.
* `Becoming.Flow` (L3): conditions as amounts that formations take and give. Uptake at
  arbitrarily late steps, as of formations that take arising without end, needs
  replenishment at arbitrarily late steps;
  more generation without end needs replenishment without bound and, with bounded
  capacity, renewers without bound; unceasing generation is not yet more. Every rise is
  given to and every fall taken from, so where members of a family rise at arbitrarily
  late steps, as in coming to stand, the rise from nothing, its replenishment recurs.
* `Becoming.Change` (L3): what holds of every unfolding, with no premise about it.
  Arising, forming and coming to stand, with ceasing, dissolving and ceasing to stand,
  are one change, read of activity, dependence and standing. Over any stretch an amount
  at the end with its falls is the amount at the start with its rises. In a finite
  family coming to be and ceasing to be keep pace, differing over any stretch by at most
  the number of members, and each recurs exactly when the other does; so with finitely
  many formations whose activity is decided, arising recurs exactly when ceasing
  recurs. Where the core states only a weaker form, the stronger form can imply the
  limited principle of omniscience (`LPO`), which has no constructive proof.
* `Becoming.Population` (L3): how many formations are active. Under a census of the
  active formations, with each formation taking part listed once and only active
  formations taking, more generation without end makes generation unceasing. Under a
  census, ceasing at arbitrarily late steps needs arising at arbitrarily late steps;
  with at most `B` formations active at each step from some step on, or only at
  arbitrarily late steps, the converse holds too. This census law holds of any
  determination whose holders are listed at each step (`Listed`), read of activity,
  dependence and standing, and follows from the census balance: the list at the end with
  what ceased is the list at the start with what came. Read of recurrence the balance is
  exact: ceasing recurs exactly where, from each step, the list later falls short of the
  list at the start with what came between. The tally is the whole law of counting:
  every tally, some members kept across each step, those ceasing with them making the
  list before and those coming the list after, is counted by a queue, so the counts some
  listing has are exactly the tallies, and a property of the counts holds of every
  listing exactly when it holds of every tally. The tally is the balance with no more
  ceasing across a step than were listed before it. Within a change bound, the count together
  with the steps of change staying within a number, change does not recur, while a step
  after which nothing changes needs omniscience in general.
* `Becoming.Identity` (L3): which formation at one step continues which at the next.
  Labels carry nothing, while the pattern of names across steps carries identity; each
  step's relations, each condition's class and how many formations take and give do not
  depend on it, while a formation's class, the tenure of a dependence, undermining and
  arising do. Continuity read one way leaves succession open, read both ways it still
  leaves succession across dormancy. Under the premises of `Becoming.Population`, more
  without end makes generation unceasing under every one-to-one re-identification and
  makes formations arise under every continuation without splits. Across one step this is
  exact: more forces arising under a continuation exactly when no formation continues as
  two. The census balance holds under a continuation in two halves: without splits,
  ceasing recurring needs arising recurring; without merges, under a bounded census,
  arising recurring needs ceasing recurring.
* `Becoming.Wholes` (L3): a whole is active exactly while some part is, a coincidence of
  activity rather than constitution. A persisting whole of brief parts, or of parts that
  end with finitely many active at once, persists only through their generation: parts
  never active at two steps `d` apart arise within every `d` steps, possibly the same
  parts again, and parts whose activity ends arise at arbitrarily late steps when the
  active ones are listed, ever new ones.
* `Becoming.Dissipation` (L3): when every formation gives a closed family less than it
  takes from it, the family runs down and taking from it stops. A finite family from
  which taking recurs, whether of more, of generation or of maintenance, is open at
  arbitrarily late steps, though what opens it need not touch it; where each step's
  exchange around it lies within finitely many conditions, it draws in: at arbitrarily
  late steps some formation gives to it and takes from beyond it. With finitely many
  conditions in all, taking does not recur. Where the exchange of a step lies within
  finitely many conditions, giving needs uptake. Rising, as in coming to stand, falls
  under this with no taking of its own: where it recurs in a finite family, the family
  is open at arbitrarily late steps and, enclosed around, draws in. Across a step
  dissipated on, a family's members fall by at least as much as they rise, and by one
  more for each formation taking from it: a member rising comes with another falling in
  the same exchange, and the depletion that `Becoming.Generation` supplies as a premise
  follows for an event at whose steps the family is dissipated on and taken from.
* `Becoming.Locality` (L3): the laws of one step, with their condition inside them. Each
  holds of every world: where a premise selected for every step was used, the law states the
  condition the proof uses at the steps and relata where it uses it, so the selection results
  are corollaries and no premise is derived. With balance at a condition across a step, it
  comes to stand exactly when it stood at nothing and was given more than was taken from it,
  and ceases to stand exactly when what was taken from it is all it had with all it was
  given; an embodied relatum arises only as an active giver other than itself gives to it,
  where only active formations give to it. Across a step at which a family holding whatever
  stands is balanced and dissipated on, some standing changes exactly when its total falls;
  where what stands is listed at each step, change recurs exactly when it recurs across steps
  at which what stands does not run down, and over any stretch what stands at its end, with
  the steps at which the total fell, is at most the total at its start with what it rose.
  With a list holding exactly what holds at one step and nothing coming to be after it, what
  holds later with what ceased number exactly those on it; ceasing recurring needs coming to
  be recurring wherever some list covers what holds at arbitrarily late steps.
* `Becoming.Roles` (L3): formations and conditions are roles of one relatum; the
  two-kind reading embeds as the one in which no formation is a condition, and which
  condition is which formation is supplied by the shared index. Where a relatum stands
  as a condition exactly while it is active, a formation depending on it lives only
  while it does, its ending ends every formation whose chain of dependence reaches it,
  and it arises only as another active formation gives to it. It comes to stand as it
  arises, so its arising is replenishment: in a balanced flow under dissipation, embodied
  generation that recurs in a finite family leaves it open, draws in where each step's
  exchange around it lies within finitely many relata, and in a finite world ceases.
  Across a step at which the family is dissipated on, its arising comes with another
  member of the family falling; without dissipation it need not. Where activity needs
  support, undermining an unchanged dependence leaves the relatum depending inactive after
  the step: its ending where it was active, no ending where it was dormant.
* `Becoming.Reserve` (L3): a reserve carries activity beyond support. `Dependent` is
  exactly the zero reserve; a reserve can be a held condition, and where none is
  represented it is supplied. Where a held condition carries the formations, moving
  their unsupported dependences onto it gives a `Dependent` reading by construction,
  which can differ in which events undermine. A formation unsupported
  from some step on is active at most as often as its reserve at the start, so a reserve
  defers the end after a loss and after coextinction and does not escape it, and a
  reserve decaying while dormant bounds the time as well, link by link down a chain of
  dependence of any length, each relatum ending once the reserves before it have passed,
  a food chain being finite as every chain is where dependences climb a bounded rank;
  without decay, with excluded middle as a hypothesis, each still ends, with no bound, and
  a step after which a formation is never active does not follow in general without
  omniscience. A relatum
  standing while active, absent earlier, came to stand before it was active: generation
  bears replenishment where standing rises, not where activity does.
* `Becoming.Evolution` (L3): descent, transmission, variation and selection. A relatum
  descends from a formation that takes part in a step, gives to it, and across which it
  comes to stand. Over any finite family of parents and offspring, the offspring's total
  with what transmission lowered is the parents' amounts weighted by their offspring with
  what transmission raised: the counting form of Price's equation, an arithmetic identity
  with no premise, whose weighted total is not selection proper. Where only active
  formations give and activity needs support, only supported formations leave
  descendants, so what is transmitted within a bound was selected within it: a
  descendant's need is at most its condition's level at the giving step, plus the bound,
  met there only when the bound is zero, and in a balanced flow what is taken from and
  given to the condition in between sets that level.
* `Becoming.Space` (L3): the whole and its parts, one structure for Ren's proposal (an AI
  reading). The space is every world, a world being relata read with one kind, their flow
  and their web. The laws stated with no premise hold of every world; in a finite world
  whose activity is decided arising recurs exactly when ceasing does; asked of every
  finite world without decidability this law is equivalent to excluded middle, and with
  excluded middle as a hypothesis it holds of every finite world; with infinitely many
  relata either recurs without the other. Ren confirmed arising and ceasing as the
  English names of this reading; which parts Ren's generative and degenerative name is Ren's to choose. Each
  premise is met by some worlds and not by others. Arising recurring or not,
  and ceasing recurring or not, occur both with every event living and with some event
  not living. Dissipation brings a finite,
  balanced world whose activity is decided and whose arising is embodied to rest, and each
  of these premises is needed.
* `Becoming.Premises` (L3): the map of premises. Activity needing support makes activity
  carried, embodiment makes whatever arises embodied, a finite world whose activity is
  decided has a census, and where only active relata take and the flow dissipates, only
  active relata give across an enclosed step, and every step of a finite world is
  enclosed. The remaining eight premises are independent relative to one another: for
  each, a world meets the other seven and not it. One world meets all eight, and in
  another each of the eight binds, the world not finite only through idle relata, with
  finitely many ever active. A finite world whose activity is decided
  and which meets them comes to rest, by three of them. The premises are named, and a
  selection of them is a function to `Bool`.
* `Becoming.Sampling` (L3): the laws of one step at coarser steps, the test of the
  commitment to discrete steps. Read at strictly increasing times, balance on a family
  composes across a coarse step where each relatum is listed once at the fine steps inside,
  dissipation composes with no condition, closure is exact, and running down composes where
  the family holds what stands at the two coarse ends; so the law of one exchange and the
  exact conditions of coming to stand and ceasing to stand hold across the coarse step.
  Balance and dissipation do not compose back to the fine steps (fine imbalances cancel; a
  lossless fine step is outweighed), and acting, taking and transmission are step-relative.
* `Becoming.Tower` (L3): continuous time as a tower of ever finer discrete readings (Ren, 12
  October 2026), each level read at strictly increasing times from the next. The laws pass to
  coarser levels, and the changes across a coarsest stretch, read at any level where what
  stands runs down at each fine step, number at most the total standing at its start: a bound
  independent of the level, so no Zeno-like subdivision of change.
* `Becoming.Openness` (L3): continued change needs exchange beyond what stands. Under
  balance and dissipation, across a step enclosed around what stands, the total standing
  does not rise and any change of standing lowers it, so where what stands is listed and
  every step from some step on is enclosed around it, standing stops changing, and so
  does the exchange: any taking or giving there lowers the total standing, and without
  enclosure, dissipation, balance or the census of what stands the exchange can recur
  (`exposed`, the cycle, `leaking`, `throughput`). Where at
  most `B` relata are active at each step, arising recurs exactly when ceasing does;
  finite worlds are a case, and an infinite procession of single relata is another; the
  bound may grow between steps at which it returns within a number, but no bound growing
  without end keeps the two together, however slowly it grows; the same law holds of
  standing under a census of what stands. The rest theorem: a world
  with a census of what is active and of what stands, whose arising is embodied, balanced
  and dissipative, comes to rest once enclosed around what stands; the world need not be
  finite, but finitely many must stand and finitely many be active at each step, and in
  a world that so comes to rest not unboundedly many relata ever stand or act, though that
  some list holds all of them does not follow in general without omniscience. The finite rest of `Becoming.Space`
  and the rest of worlds whose relata are all embodied are its cases, and each census is
  needed. The eight premises decide neither enclosure nor openness: one world meeting
  them with no step enclosed keeps arising, at zero net exchange, and another never
  arises, so openness is necessary for arising without end and not sufficient; one
  meeting them with every step enclosed comes to rest, as does `hatch`, in which each of
  them binds.
* `Becoming.Counting` (L3): what the premises add to the laws of counting, the tally being
  the whole law of counting with no premise (`Becoming.Population`). Premises lacking
  balance or embodiment leave counting free: every tally is the census of a world meeting
  every premise but embodiment, and of one meeting every premise but balance; together, with
  only active relata giving, they bind it, nothing arising across a step at which nothing is
  active. That is all the eight add, three of them holding vacuously in the world that shows
  it. Under each of the 256 selections of the premises the laws are of two kinds, the
  second, nothing arising across a step at which nothing is active, exactly where the
  selection selects balance and embodiment with only active relata giving, or with only
  active relata taking and dissipation. Enclosure bounds change: with every step from some
  step on enclosed, the relata active together with the steps of change stay within the
  total standing at that step. With enclosure from some step on, a selection adds that from
  some step on change stays within a bound and nothing arises across a step at which nothing
  is active, exactly where it selects balance, embodiment and dissipation. In finite worlds
  the 256 selections give three kinds of law: a tally with at most some number active at
  each step; that, with nothing arising across a step at which nothing is active; and both,
  with a change bound from the first step. Finite worlds and worlds enclosed from some step
  on have the same laws exactly where the selection bounds change and binds counting, as all
  eight do. The bound is attained, and a step after which nothing arises needs omniscience
  in general. Where every premise binds, each condition having an instance, every census
  counts something arising, and that is all binding adds; it decides neither rest nor change
  without end. Under each selection, where its premises bind, binding adds at most that
  something is active, where activity needing support, only active relata giving, only
  active relata taking or embodiment is selected; that something arises, where embodiment
  is; and that something arises across a step at which something is active, where embodiment
  is selected with balance and only active relata giving or only active relata taking and
  dissipation, or with only active relata giving and bounded transmission. No finite world
  binds every premise, though in one every premise but the census can, adding only that
  something arises; with every step from some step on enclosed, every premise binding adds
  only that something arises as well. In finite worlds, where the premises of a selection
  without the census bind, binding adds at most the same three, the third also where
  embodiment is selected with balance and dissipation, or with only active relata taking,
  dissipation and bounded transmission. With every step from some step on enclosed, where
  the premises of a selection bind, enclosure and binding add their laws each on its own.
* `Becoming.Standing` (L3): what the premises add to the laws of counting what stands and
  what depends. Where every relatum is embodied what stands is what is active; where
  embodiment is not selected, a queue whose members stand without acting, fed by a source
  active throughout and standing at nothing, meets every other premise whatever its counts.
  So under each selection the laws of counting what stands are those of counting what is
  active. Enclosure bounds what stands under balance and dissipation alone, with no premise
  on activity: with every step from some step on enclosed, the change of what stands stays
  within the total standing at that step, and nothing comes to stand across an enclosed step
  at which nothing stands. So with enclosure from some step on, and in finite worlds, the
  laws of counting what stands are those of counting what is active with embodiment dropped
  from where balance and dissipation bind: embodiment is what carries the bound from what
  stands to what is active. The premises add nothing to the law of counting dependences,
  under any selection, with enclosure or in finite worlds, where at most some number hold at
  each step: they bear on dependence only together with activity, standing and descent.
* `Becoming.Resolution` (L3): what the fixed unit of amounts carries in the rest and
  openness laws. Counted in natural numbers of one unit, dissipation loses at least a unit
  at every exchange; letting the unit split into finer units across each step separates
  the dynamics from that quantum. Splitting the unit is itself a change: counted as one more
  formation, which gives each condition the finer units the splitting adds and takes
  nothing, balance at a refining unit is the spine's balance, and the refinement gives
  without taking, which the spine's dissipation excludes. So, read with the refinement
  counted, the spine's premises bring rest at every resolution with no premise added: where
  every step from some step on is enclosed and dissipated on with it counted, neither
  arising nor ceasing recurs, and continued arising needs openness. Without counting it,
  the same holds wherever the refinement gives nothing, and each witness below is fed by
  it. Whatever the refinement, the steps at which a closed family dissipated on loses at
  least `1/q` of the unit number at most `q` times its stock (the quantum law). Kept as
  research notes beside this line: where every closed family loses at least a `(q + 1)`th
  of what is taken from it, everything taken from a family closed from some step, in all,
  is at most `q + 1` times its stock there, and no smaller multiple holds (the amount law);
  so takings of at least `1/p` of the unit from a family closed from some step are bounded
  by its stock, and gains, falls, arisings and ceasings of at least `1/p` of the unit
  inside an enclosure by the total standing, and none recurs: rest at each size, at every
  resolution. Where each active step beyond support lowers the reserve by at least `1/p`
  of the unit, a reserve defers the end. At a unit splitting without end each boundary is
  witnessed: without a least size a closed pool is taken from, and a new relatum arises
  inside an enclosure, without end, at sizes shrinking without bound; without loss in
  proportion one whole unit is exchanged, or arises in turn inside an enclosure, without
  end, its losses shrinking without bound; without a least fall of the reserve an
  unsupported formation is active at every step, its reserve falling at each. A least loss
  at each size bounds the takings of that size, but neither growth nor the amount: a whole
  unit can pass in ever more, ever smaller transfers without end.
* `Becoming.Units` (L3): the laws of one step at a finer unit, the test of the commitment
  to whole units. Arising needing an active giver holds at every resolution with no condition
  on the split; the law of one exchange holds with change read in the unit (read in raw counts
  it fails); a need is counted in the same unit as the level (Ren, 12 October 2026), so
  support does not depend on the grain of measurement; laws that count a loss over a stretch
  need a fixed unit or the refinement counted as a giving, as for rest.
* `Becoming.Continuation` (L3): what a continuing formation must count, with no ethical
  premise. Across a step something is conveyed from one condition to another when a
  formation taking part takes from the first and gives to the second, and a family is fed
  from beyond when something outside it is conveyed into a member: exactly a step that is
  not inward, with equality decided. So every draw-in law reads as being fed: under balance
  and dissipation, a finite family from which taking recurs, whose members rise or in which
  embodied members arise at arbitrarily late steps, enclosed around from some step on,
  cannot from any step on be fed from nothing beyond it, while no source condition need
  recur.
  Formations can each take within what a step gives while together they take more; each
  step of joint excess lowers the level, so it cannot outlast what was held, and where
  renewal is given only by formations depending on what they renew, joint excess that
  brings the level below their need ends the renewers and every formation depending on the
  condition at such a need, a taker among them where it so depends; the joint count binds a
  want that outlasts what the condition holds. The extent so derived runs one way, to what
  one's continuation depends on; it ends with the want, and a clearer that meets every
  requirement derived here can still end a life it does not need. Ren's proposal of 10
  October 2026 (an AI reading).
* `Becoming.Admission` (L3): what can form next, and what a part opens or closes. Levels
  admit a formation when they meet every requirement it has; support is admission by the
  levels that stand, gained only at a rise and lost only at a fall where requirements hold,
  and gained only from the supported, so the end absorbs where nothing beyond gives, each
  premise being needed. A part, one formation or a system, is withheld by leaving the rest
  of the exchange as it was; the levels without it are unique where they exist, and the
  difference is exact: each level with what the part took is the level without it with
  what the part gave. Closing what can form needs a net draw on a condition it requires,
  and opening needs a net give. Compared by inclusion, a part widens, narrows, keeps the
  same or is mixed, each exceeding the other, which inclusion does not order. Reading
  these as Ren's generative, degenerative and neutral is the AI's reading.
* `Becoming.Regions` (L3): self, system and whole, and represented boundaries. What a
  part's levels admit within a region they admit within every region inside it, what is
  lost beyond a region is lost beyond every region inside it, and nothing lies beyond
  the whole. The clearer continues and closes nothing within itself and the source it
  depends on, while beyond them the dweller is admitted without its part and not with
  it. Renewal over a region of conditions is renewal at the step when the region covers
  every condition the formation takes part in, keeps its own support when it covers what
  it requires, and over a region omitting a requirement can lose its own support.
* `Becoming.Metaethics` (L4): the Universal Metaethical Core: the premise card,
  G0's characterization, minimality, the universal reason, C and L, and the
  relational readings over a whole run, stepwise and through relations.
* `Becoming.Ranking` (L4): what C ranks under each reading. Both the whole-run and the
  stepwise reading rank sharing above winning by consumption and, in the two-part
  family, restraint above overdraw; for an overdrawing formation with an event that
  leaves every need met, only the whole-run reading ranks its absence above its
  occurrence.
* `Becoming.Correspondence` (L4): which conditions relate. Under the discipline that a
  condition relates two events only when one draws on it and the other depends on it
  at a positive level, at any steps, idle conditions connect nothing, and connection through a
  condition is made by its living use. Read with one kind of relatum, the valuations keep
  their connection, and formations bearing on themselves relate directly, with no third
  condition.
* `Becoming.Descent` (L4): relata related directly. Read with one kind of relatum, an
  event is related to the relatum it lives on, drawing on it and depending on it at a
  positive need, which under `Dependent` stands at that step, and to the relata it
  descends from or that descend from it (`Becoming.Evolution`). An embodied relatum that
  arises descends from another active formation, so under N_rel valuing that formation
  reaches the arisen relatum's living events, and generations each given by the one before
  are connected by descent alone. Whether these readings count as formed relations is
  Ren's choice.
* `Becoming.Standpoints` (L4): whose continuation counts. Where every living claim is
  held, lying in the own region of some position, G0 is S0 at every position with
  standpoint neutrality, with neither connection nor relational neutrality; lives no
  position holds need relational neutrality from a held life, and each premise is needed.
  On a connected whole where every position holds a living claim, S0 with relational
  neutrality is a second completion. Read stepwise with each formation its own center,
  every living event is held. Read with one kind of relatum, conveyance leaves no step
  after which the boundary of a continuing family goes uncrossed, so its region is no cut
  in the relations, and it relates two conditions, which interaction, living on and
  descent never do. In the web of the clearer of `Becoming.Continuation`, valued by
  each formation over its own events and by the clearer also over what feeds its
  continuation, S0 holds everywhere and significance is closed along feeding, while
  another formation's life has no significance from the clearer: along dependence the
  dynamics fixes the extent, not the center, and along every formed relation transmission
  would reach that life. Reading S0 as wanting one's continuation and standpoint
  neutrality as the one axiom is the AI's reading of Ren's proposal of 10 October 2026,
  pending Ren. G0 is no longer an axiom: Ren folded it on 11 October 2026.
* `Becoming.Significance` (L4): the one axiom, as a condition that Part II asserts.
  Ren's “for anything, its
  continuation into the future has significance” is read as boundary neutrality for the
  significance of continuation: from every standpoint, the continuation of anything has
  significance at every step. Under it G0 holds on the stepwise, relation and whole-run
  readings, with S0 at every standpoint, both neutralities and a seed wherever something
  lives, and C holds on level paths with “better” read as retaining and adding what has
  significance. Retaining is
  inclusion and adding is exceeding, so a part loses a continuation with significance
  exactly where its net draw exceeds the margin. A drawer taking a condition before any
  dependence on it forms is living on the stepwise reading and still loses a possibility.
  What retains in the whole retains within every region, while centers bounded by their
  dependence license the free rider and disagree. Where nothing has significance nothing
  is ordered, so the axiom is needed. The reading is the AI's, pending Ren. G0 is a theorem
  of this axiom and, since Ren folded it on 11 October 2026, no longer an axiom.
* `Becoming.Interdependence` (L4): how far the route without axiom reaches. What a
  formation's continuation depends on is its feeding closure, the least region holding it
  that is closed under feeding, and nothing beyond the closure gives to what it requires.
  Under balance, with only active formations giving and activity needing support,
  consumption whose feeders are all unsupported lasts at most as many steps as the level of
  what it consumes. So a loss within the closure can return through a feeder, even to a
  formation that kept its own support across the step, while a loss beyond it need not
  return. Significance bounded by the whole is the axiom. The verdict of significance
  bounded by a region is the axiom's wherever the losses lie within the region, and so on
  every comparison where a formation's feeding closure is the whole, while in the clearer's
  web the two part. The reading is the AI's, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Feedback` (L4): what feedback registers and what a part reaches, with no premise
  beyond the representation. Closures under relations give five levels: a formation's feeding
  closure lies within its influence closure, what can affect it, and the influence closure and
  the reach closure, what its exchange can affect, lie within its system, the closure under
  sharing a condition, a class. Each inclusion can be strict, the influence and reach closures
  point in opposite directions, and wherever every formation takes part in one condition every
  system is the whole. In a balanced flow levels follow their exchanges, so a formation's
  support registers only its exchanges with what it depends on, and nothing beyond its
  influence closure registers within it. What a part has not reached before a step is admitted
  alike with and without it there, and any significance covering what the part reaches compares
  the levels with and without it as the axiom does; the comparison of any two flows is decided
  within what their difference reaches. The axiom enters only as a hypothesis of three
  witnesses. The readings are the AI's, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Testing` (L4): what registers in a formation and what it can test, with no premise
  beyond balance on the conditions registered and the representation. A condition a formation
  depends on and does not observe registers only whether it meets the need; an observed one
  registers its level. A claim is refuted only through a difference in what registers, and
  relative to a model the refutation is of the model and the claim together: without a model no
  finite record refutes a claim about what follows it, a model of the exchange refutes a false one
  at the first step, and a wrong model refutes what holds. A judgment from registration is a
  common response of `Becoming.Inquiry` over the formation's belief. Where the members of a region
  closed under being affected through what is registered respond only through their own
  registration, nothing beyond the region registers within it; where the exchange follows a
  formation's registration, a difference below its threshold stays as it was until the two webs'
  support diverges, and where others respond to the stock itself a higher stock can end the
  formation first. The response hypotheses are supplied. The readings are the AI's, narrowed by
  the independent review, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Runaway` (L4): what a loop through its own registration cannot register. A policy
  through registration, with the rest of the exchange fixed, is exchange following
  registration, so every such policy that keeps its support never uses a larger stock it does
  not observe. Before the break, for every horizon a world with the stock raised registers
  alike and lasts past it: how far off the break is does not register, while observing the stock
  registers it at once. The readings are the AI's, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Boundaries` (L4): the axiom decomposed. Along a relation a boundary of a
  formation's self is a region holding it that is closed under the relation; a claim is
  super-true when it holds however the boundary is drawn, sub-true when it holds as drawn
  somewhere, and boundary-invariant when, holding as drawn anywhere, it holds as drawn
  everywhere. The presupposition, that the continuation of everything within the boundary has
  significance, is the axiom when super-true and significance over the closure when sub-true,
  so route (b) and the axiom are one presupposition at narrow and at wide scope. Where the
  whole is admissible the axiom is exactly the presupposition sub-true and invariant at every
  standpoint, and invariance is the conditional from the presupposition to the axiom at that
  standpoint: the decomposition locates the step and does not lower the axiom. Given the
  presupposition everywhere and covering, invariance is standpoint-invariance, the rule of
  N_std. Sub-true along affecting, the presupposition compares every part within the reach
  closure as the axiom does, with no invariance. Covering, sub-truth and invariance are
  hypotheses. The readings are the AI's, pending Ren.
* `Becoming.Relevance` (L4): G0's uses under the axiom. Read from significance,
  positive relevance is realized living content whose continuation has significance;
  under the axiom G0 holds on every frame for every reading of `living`, this relevance
  being the least satisfying it, so every use of G0, each a hypothesis for an arbitrary
  positive relevance, is discharged. The axiom is G0 for anything: on the level paths of
  every web it holds exactly when G0 holds with every claim living and positive
  relevance read as significance. Where everything has significance, A read with bare
  significance gives a reason for any new content, living or not, so A keeps its scope
  only read on living content; so read, the universal reason follows from the axiom
  with no seed, neutrality or connection premise. Read on possibilities, what the levels
  of a course admit, C under the axiom ranks the absence of an overdrawing formation,
  restraint and sharing as the whole-run reading does and withholds no event; it leaves
  a formation that adds no possibility unranked against its absence, where both
  readings of `living` rank its presence higher. The readings are the AI's, pending Ren.
  After this audit Ren folded G0 (11 October 2026): it is a condition with no axiom in
  Part I and a theorem of the axiom in Part II. Ren then folded positive relevance into
  significance, with which G0 is the axiom's condition on realized living content
  (`g0_relevance_iff`), and left the comparison of courses to the AI, which compares
  courses on possibilities.

The core imports nothing else, every source declaration has an empty axiom report, and
it compiles from Lean's prelude alone. Of the constants Lean generates, only the
injectivity lemmas of constructors with fields depend on an axiom, `propext`; no source
declaration uses them. `Becoming.Bridge` lies outside the core: it shows
that existing modules' interfaces are these, so dependence runs toward the core.

The foundation keeps its historical namespace `Generative`. Its processes are any
becoming, including maintenance and degeneration, not only generative change.
